       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DA2FUNTEXT.
      *> DA2 - A NUMERIC INTRINSIC FUNCTION IS LEGAL WHEREVER THE
      *> STANDARD WRITES "IDENTIFIER-N": 8.4.3.1.2 FORMAT 1 MAKES
      *> FUNCTION-IDENTIFIER-1 AN IDENTIFIER, AND 14.9.11.3 SR1
      *> EXCLUDES ONLY MESSAGE-TAG, OBJECT AND POINTER. BEFORE THIS,
      *> ONLY THE COMPILE-TIME-FOLDED CASES WORKED.
      *>
      *> ⛔ THE CENTRAL FACT: THE FOLD MUST NOT BE OBSERVABLE.
      *> AN INTRINSIC OVER LITERAL/CONSTANT ARGUMENTS FOLDS TO A
      *> NUMERIC LITERAL; ONE OVER A RUNTIME ARGUMENT DOES NOT. THE
      *> TWO MUST PRINT IDENTICALLY OR THE OPTIMIZATION HAS BECOME
      *> USER-VISIBLE. LINES 1/2 AND 3/4 ARE THOSE PAIRS: SAME VALUE,
      *> ONE FOLDED AND ONE COMPUTED, SO THEY MUST MATCH EXACTLY.
      *>
      *> 15.4 PUTS A RETURNED VALUE IN A "TEMPORARY ELEMENTARY DATA
      *> ITEM" WHOSE CHARACTERISTICS ARE IMPLEMENTOR-DEFINED UNDER
      *> NATIVE ARITHMETIC (15.4.1), AND 14.9.11.4 GR1 MAKES THE
      *> DISPLAY CONVERSION IMPLEMENTOR-DEFINED TOO. COBOL.NET'S
      *> DETERMINATION (docs/CONFORMANCE.md, ANNEX A.1) IS THE
      *> LITERAL FORM: SIGNIFICANT DIGITS, NO ZERO PADDING, LEADING
      *> "-" WHEN NEGATIVE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 G     PIC X(5).
       01 C     PIC X VALUE "A".
       01 FIVE  PIC 9 VALUE 5.
       01 A     PIC X(10).
       01 SGN   PIC S9(3) VALUE -14.
      *> TWO DIGITS, SO ITS DE-SIGNED IMAGE IS "14" AND NOT "014" -
      *> THAT ISOLATES THE *SIGN* RULE IN THE COMPARISON BELOW FROM
      *> THE UNRELATED WIDTH DIFFERENCE. A DECLARED ITEM PADS TO ITS
      *> PICTURE; A FUNCTION RESULT HAS NO PICTURE TO PAD TO.
       01 SGN2  PIC S99 VALUE -14.
       01 TXT   PIC X(10) VALUE "14".
       01 R     PIC 9V9(12) VALUE 0.
       01 U     PIC 9V99 VALUE 0.
       01 SV    PIC S9V99 VALUE 0.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> PAIR ONE - THE VALUE 5, FOLDED THEN COMPUTED.
           DISPLAY FUNCTION LENGTH(G)
           DISPLAY FUNCTION MAX(FIVE 3)
      *> PAIR TWO - THE VALUE 7, FOLDED THEN COMPUTED.
           DISPLAY FUNCTION MAX(3 7)
           DISPLAY FUNCTION MAX(FIVE 7)
      *> 15.70.1 - THE ORDINAL POSITION IN THE PROGRAM COLLATING
      *> SEQUENCE, LOWEST POSITION 1. "A" IS 65 NATIVE, SO 66.
           DISPLAY FUNCTION ORD(C)
      *> A NEGATIVE RESULT CARRIES A LEADING MINUS, NEVER AN
      *> OVERPUNCH - THIS IS NOT A STORED ZONED ITEM.
           DISPLAY FUNCTION MIN(3 -14 0 8 -3)
      *> AND IN A MULTI-OPERAND DISPLAY, WHERE THE OPERAND IS
      *> CONCATENATED RATHER THAN SENT ALONE (14.9.11.4 GR6).
           DISPLAY "[" FUNCTION ORD(C) "]"
      *> THE SAME OPERAND RULE APPLIES TO A MOVE WITH AN
      *> ALPHANUMERIC RECEIVER: 14.9.25.4 GR6 TREATS THE SENDING
      *> NUMERIC AS THOUGH MOVED TO AN ALPHANUMERIC ITEM, SO THE
      *> TEXT IS LEFT-JUSTIFIED AND SPACE-FILLED IN PIC X(10).
           MOVE FUNCTION ORD(C) TO A
           DISPLAY "[" A "]"
      *> ⛔ 14.9.25.4 GR6a - "IF THE SENDING OPERAND IS DESCRIBED AS
      *> BEING SIGNED NUMERIC, THE OPERATIONAL SIGN IS NOT MOVED."
      *> A GENERAL RULE WITH NO IMPLEMENTOR LATITUDE: THE 15.4.1 /
      *> 14.9.11.4 GR1 LATITUDE COVERS THE FORM OF THE TEXT, NOT
      *> WHETHER THE SIGN TRAVELS. SO A *NEGATIVE* FUNCTION RESULT
      *> MOVED TO A PIC X RECEIVER LOSES ITS SIGN - EXACTLY AS A
      *> SIGNED ITEM DOES - WHILE DISPLAY, WHICH IS NOT A DE-SIGNING
      *> CONTEXT, STILL SHOWS IT. THE FIRST CUT OF THIS GOLDEN USED
      *> ONLY THE POSITIVE ORD, SO IT PASSED EITHER WAY.
           MOVE SGN TO A
           DISPLAY "SI=[" A "]"
           MOVE FUNCTION MIN(3 -14 0) TO A
           DISPLAY "SF=[" A "]"
           DISPLAY "SD=[" FUNCTION MIN(3 -14 0) "]"
      *> AND THE SAME RULE ON THE TEXT-RELATION PATH (8.8.4.2.5
      *> ROUTES AN ALPHANUMERIC/NUMERIC COMPARE THROUGH MOVE RULES):
      *> BOTH SIDES MUST AGREE.
           IF TXT = SGN2 DISPLAY "CI=EQ" ELSE DISPLAY "CI=NE" END-IF
           IF TXT = FUNCTION MIN(3 -14 0)
               DISPLAY "CF=EQ" ELSE DISPLAY "CF=NE" END-IF
      *> ⛔ AN INTRINSIC'S WORKING SCALE IS max(Receiver.Scale, 9),
      *> AND THE RENDERER'S RECEIVER IS PER-UNIT MUTABLE STATE. AN
      *> ADD THAT DID NOT RESTORE IT LEFT ITS RECEIVER LATCHED, SO
      *> THIS SECOND SQRT PRINTED MORE DIGITS THAN THE FIRST. A
      *> FUNCTION'S TEXT MUST NOT DEPEND ON A PRECEDING STATEMENT.
           DISPLAY "Q1=[" FUNCTION SQRT(4) "]"
           ADD 1 TO R
           DISPLAY "Q2=[" FUNCTION SQRT(4) "]"
      *> ⛔ THE FOLD PATH USES THE SAME TEXT RULE, BY DELEGATION AND
      *> NOT BY A SECOND COPY. THE COPY HAD DRIFTED: IT RETURNED "0"
      *> FOR A ZERO MAGNITUDE AND DROPPED THE SCALE, SO THE LOWEST
      *> VALUE OF AN UNSIGNED 9V99 ITEM FOLDED TO "0" RATHER THAN
      *> "0.00" - A LITERAL AT THE WRONG SCALE, WHICH THEN FEEDS
      *> WHATEVER ARITHMETIC USES IT (15.58.4 / ANNEX D.32).
           DISPLAY "LU=[" FUNCTION LOWEST-ALGEBRAIC(U) "]"
           DISPLAY "LS=[" FUNCTION LOWEST-ALGEBRAIC(SV) "]"
           DISPLAY "HU=[" FUNCTION HIGHEST-ALGEBRAIC(U) "]"
           DISPLAY "SM=[" FUNCTION SMALLEST-ALGEBRAIC(U) "]"
           STOP RUN.
